  <!-- JAMB General FAQ -->
  <div class="faq-container">
    <h2>JAMB: Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>1. How much is the JAMB registration form?</summary>
      <p>The cost of the JAMB form is <strong>₦4,700</strong>. This includes the ePIN and the official JAMB-recommended reading text. Additional charges may apply if paid through agents or banks.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>2. Can I register for JAMB myself online?</summary>
      <p><strong>No.</strong> Registration must be done at a JAMB-accredited CBT center. This ensures proper biometric data capture and secure, standardized registration. Self-registration is not accepted and may lead to disqualification.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>3. Is JAMB required for all tertiary institutions?</summary>
      <p>Yes, most Nigerian universities and polytechnics require JAMB for admission. However, some private institutions and foreign academic programs may offer alternative routes or entrance exams that do not require JAMB.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>4. Can I gain admission without JAMB?</summary>
      <p>Yes, you can gain admission without JAMB through the following options:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>JUPEB (Joint Universities Preliminary Examinations Board)</li>
        <li>IJMB (Interim Joint Matriculation Board)</li>
        <li>Pre-degree or foundation programs</li>
        <li>Some private universities offer Direct Entry admission options</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>5. How do I check my JAMB result?</summary>
      <p>
        You can check your result using two methods:<br/><br/>
        <strong>Via JAMB Portal:</strong><br/>
        - Go to <a href="https://www.jamb.gov.ng" target="_blank">https://www.jamb.gov.ng</a><br/>
        - Click on “Check UTME Result”<br/>
        - Enter your registration number or email<br/>
        - Click “Check My Result”<br/><br/>
        <strong>Via SMS:</strong><br/>
        - Send <strong>UTMERESULT</strong> to <strong>55019</strong> using your registered SIM.<br/>
        - Standard SMS charges apply.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>6. How do I retrieve my JAMB registration number?</summary>
      <p>You can retrieve your JAMB registration number by logging into your JAMB profile via the official portal or by contacting the CBT center where you registered. Always ensure your login credentials are safely stored.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>7. When is JAMB reprinting starting?</summary>
      <p>JAMB reprinting typically begins <strong>a week before the exam</strong>. This allows candidates to check their specific exam date, time, and venue. You must reprint your slip from the JAMB portal or at your CBT center to get these details.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>8. How can I download the JAMB syllabus?</summary>
      <p>
        The JAMB syllabus is an essential guide that outlines the topics you are expected to study for each subject. To download the syllabus:
        <br /><br />
        <strong>Official Method:</strong><br />
        Visit the official JAMB website at <a href="https://www.jamb.gov.ng" target="_blank">https://www.jamb.gov.ng</a>. Navigate to the <em>“Syllabus”</em> section. Select your subject and download the syllabus in PDF format.
        <br /><br />
        <strong>Alternative Method:</strong><br />
        You can also search online for <em>“JAMB 2025 Syllabus PDF download”</em> to find it on educational blogs or verified platforms. Ensure you use a trusted source.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>9. How many times can I take JAMB?</summary>
      <p>
        There is <strong>no official limit</strong> to how many times you can register for JAMB. You can take the exam every year, as long as you meet the registration requirements such as having valid O’level results and a NIN (National Identification Number).
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>10. Can I change my course or institution after JAMB?</summary>
      <p>
        <strong>Yes</strong>, JAMB allows candidates to change their course or institution after the exam. This process is called the <em>Change of Course/Institution</em> and is typically available once results are released.
        <br /><br />
        To make changes, you’ll need:
        <ul>
          <li>A JAMB profile</li>
          <li>Access to the JAMB portal</li>
          <li>A payment of around ₦2,500</li>
        </ul>
        Be sure to research the new course or institution’s requirements before applying the change.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>11. What is the minimum score to gain admission?</summary>
      <p>
        The minimum JAMB score required for admission varies by institution and course. However, the general benchmark is:
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Universities:</strong> 160–200+</li>
          <li><strong>Polytechnics:</strong> 120–150</li>
          <li><strong>Colleges of Education:</strong> 100–120</li>
        </ul>
        Note that competitive courses like Medicine, Law, and Engineering may require much higher scores. Always check with your chosen institution for their specific cut-off marks.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <!-- JAMB Data Correction FAQ -->
  <div class="faq-container">
    <h2>JAMB Correction of Data - Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary>1. What is JAMB Correction of Data?</summary>
      <p>
        JAMB Correction of Data is a service that allows candidates to correct mistakes made during UTME registration.
        This includes corrections to name, date of birth, gender, state or local government of origin (LGA), course, and institution.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>2. What types of corrections can I make on the JAMB portal?</summary>
      <ul>
        <li>Change of Name</li>
        <li>Change of Gender</li>
        <li>Change of Date of Birth</li>
        <li>Change of State or Local Government Area (LGA)</li>
        <li>Change of Course/Institution</li>
        <li>Correction of Subjects in UTME</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>3. How much does it cost to make corrections on JAMB?</summary>
      <p>The cost is usually <strong>₦2,500</strong> per correction. Additional charges from banks or online payment platforms may apply.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>4. Can I correct my name or date of birth after writing the exam?</summary>
      <p>Yes, as long as the correction portal is still open. However, changes to sensitive information like your name or date of birth may require you to upload supporting documents such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Birth Certificate</li>
        <li>Sworn Affidavit</li>
        <li>National Identification Number (NIN) printout</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>5. How many times can I change my course or institution?</summary>
      <p>JAMB allows you to change your course or institution <strong>up to two times</strong>. Each change costs ₦2,500, and you must ensure that the new institution or course matches your qualifications.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>6. Where can I do JAMB correction of data?</summary>
      <p>You can correct your JAMB data through the following methods:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>On the JAMB official portal: <a href="https://www.jamb.gov.ng" target="_blank">https://www.jamb.gov.ng</a></li>
        <li>Through your JAMB profile</li>
        <li>At any JAMB-accredited CBT center</li>
      </ul>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>7. Is the JAMB correction of data currently ongoing?</summary>
      <p>This depends on the time of the year. The correction window usually opens shortly after the UTME results are released and remains open for a few weeks. Check the official JAMB website or social media platforms for current updates.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>8. Will changing my course or institution affect my admission chances?</summary>
      <p>It might. It’s important to choose a course or institution that aligns with your UTME score and O’Level subjects. Before making any changes, research the cut-off marks and requirements or seek guidance from a school counselor.</p>
    </details>
  </div>

